## 4. Dynamic Service Templates & Subservice Builder

### Architecture & Motivation
Instead of creating rigid Mongoose models every time a new business type is added (e.g. pub, bakery, bike rental, yoga center), the dynamic engine lets admins configure schema definitions on the fly:

1. **`models/ServiceTemplate.js`**:
   - `templateName`: Human-readable name (e.g., *"Artisan Cafe & Bakery"*).
   - `category`: Base category enum (`restaurants/bars`, `hotel/resorts`, `vehicle`, `emergency`, `events`, `shopping`, `others`).
   - `subService`: Slug (e.g., `cafe`, `pub`, `car_rental`).
   - `fields`: Array of field definitions (`fieldKey`, `label`, `fieldType`, `options`, `defaultValue`, `required`, `section`).
   - `defaultPreset`: Initial JSON values for quick setup.
2. **`models/CustomService.js`**:
   - `service`: Reference to base `Service` record (ensures unified platform search).
   - `template`: Optional reference to the origin `ServiceTemplate`.
   - `title`, `category`, `subService`, `contact`, `location`.
   - `customDetails`: Dynamic key-value pairs (sanitized).
   - `fieldDefinitions`: Snapshot of schema definitions for accurate client-side form and badge rendering.
   - `status`: `"published"` (publicly visible) or `"draft"` (admin-only).
   - `photos`: MediaAsset array on Cloudflare R2.
   - `views` & `clicks`: Live analytics counters.

### Endpoints
* `POST /api/services/templates` (Admin create template)
* `GET /api/services/templates` (List templates, filter by `category`, `subService`, `search`)
* `GET /api/services/templates/:id`
* `PUT /api/services/templates/:id`
* `DELETE /api/services/templates/:id`
* `POST /api/services/templates/seed-defaults` (Seed production starter templates)
* `POST /api/services/custom` (Admin publish dynamic listing with R2 photos)
* `GET /api/services/custom` (List dynamic listings, filtered by category, subservice, status, city)
* `GET /api/services/custom/:id`
* `PUT /api/services/custom/:id`
* `DELETE /api/services/custom/:id`
* `POST /api/services/custom/:id/click` (Track 1-tap clicks/calls)

### Admin Portal Implementation
* **Page:** `buExploreAdmin/src/pages/ServiceTemplates.jsx`
* **API Client:** `buExploreAdmin/src/api/serviceTemplate.api.js`
* **Hooks:** `buExploreAdmin/src/queries/serviceTemplateQueries.js` & `buExploreAdmin/src/mutations/serviceTemplateMutation.js`
* **UI Features:**
  - **Tab 1: Subservice Templates**: Manage schemas and run "Seed Defaults" with 1 click.
  - **Tab 2: Published Custom Listings**: Pick a base template, adjust prefilled fields, dynamically add extra attributes via "+ Add Detail", or delete attributes, then upload R2 photos and publish.

