## 9. Frontend Engineer Integration Reference

### How the Frontend Renders Dynamic Listings
1. Call `GET /api/services/templates` to get available subservice templates and icons.
2. Call `GET /api/services/custom?category=restaurants/bars&subService=cafe` to fetch listings.
3. The response includes `customDetails` and `fieldDefinitions`:
   ```json
   {
     "title": "The Roasted Bean Artisan Cafe",
     "category": "restaurants/bars",
     "subService": "cafe",
     "customDetails": {
       "cuisine": ["Specialty Coffee", "Italian"],
       "avgCostForTwo": 650,
       "wifiAvailable": true,
       "liveMusic": true,
       "petFriendly": true,
       "specialRoast": "Ethiopian Yirgacheffe"
     },
     "fieldDefinitions": [
       { "fieldKey": "wifiAvailable", "label": "Wi-Fi Available", "fieldType": "boolean" },
       { "fieldKey": "liveMusic", "label": "Live Music Nights", "fieldType": "boolean" }
     ],
     "photos": [
       { "url": "https://pub-...r2.dev/services/custom/cafe/1.webp" }
     ]
   }
   ```
4. **Dynamic Rendering Rule:**
   - Iterate over `customDetails` key-value pairs.
   - If a boolean is `true`, render a badge with a checkmark or icon.
   - If an array, render tag pills.
   - If a number or string, render a label-value row.
   - Call `POST /api/services/custom/:id/click` when a user taps "Call" or "Visit Website".

